1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,460
Ever thought that satisfying pop when

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,980
you crack your knuckles as bones

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:04,820
grinding together?

4
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,020
Think again!

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,980
Inside your finger joints,

6
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:10,620
there's a lubricating fluid called synovial

7
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,000
fluid,

8
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:12,780
filled with dissolved gases.

9
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,420
When you pull your finger,

10
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,000
the joint capsule expands,

11
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:17,940
pressure drops instantly,

12
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,720
and those gases form microscopic bubbles

13
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:22,080
that collapse rapidly.

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:23,640
That sharp sound?

15
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,000
Pure physics!

16
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,160
Micro gas bubbles bursting!

17
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,500
And what about catching a yawn

18
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,720
right after someone else does?

19
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,440
Your brain's mirror neurons are wired

20
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:35,600
to instantly simulate the actions of

21
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,480
people around you.

22
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,320
Science shows that contagious yawning is

23
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,840
deeply tied to empathy.

24
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,880
You're much more likely to catch

25
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,300
a yawn from someone you care

26
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:44,620
about.

27
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,040
So why is yawning contagious?

28
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:48,640
Want to know the answer?

29
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,200
Watch our next video.

30
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,800
And don't forget to follow us

31
